    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for high offensive output today, anchored by **Kyle Tucker** (75.13) and **Jacob Wilson** (72.17). **Kyle Tucker** remains our most reliable asset against Pfaadt, benefiting from a soft SP_xERA of 4.54, while **Jacob Wilson** receives a massive boost due to a favorable wind forecast and an advantageous second-spot in the order against Bennett. Similarly, **Andy Pages** (72.12) is a high-conviction start; his projection is bolstered by the 4.54 xERA of Pfaadt and the added upside of his stolen base potential against a slow-delivery pitcher, which remains a focal point of our category strategy. Conversely, **Gunnar Henderson** (61.80) faces the toughest test of the day against deGrom. Despite the elite pedigree of the opposing arm, **Gunnar Henderson** holds his value thanks to a 14% platoon edge and the high-volume opportunities typically afforded to an elite leadoff hitter.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Sam Antonacci** (43.60), who fell just outside the playable threshold. While his leadoff role and platoon advantage against Williams were attractive, the opposing SP_xERA of 2.91 significantly suppressed his efficiency, making him a risk we aren't forced to take given our current depth. We are also closely monitoring the lineup status of **Liam Hicks** (47.11); if he is not confirmed in the #4 hole or if weather impacts the game, we may need to pivot. Investors should note the \u26a0\ufe0f rain risk currently hovering over **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (64.46). While his score is strong enough to justify the risk, the potential for a shortened outing or delay necessitates keeping a close eye on the late-afternoon radar in his matchup against Nola. We are also continuing to track injury recoveries for **Jordan Westburg** and **Josh Jung** as they remain on the IL, alongside bench reserves like **Miguel Vargas**, **Curtis Mead**, **Dominic Smith**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Luis Lara**, who are ready to plug gaps should our primary starters face unforeseen scratch scenarios.",
